{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01E7JVLBPkTPCFpoCmZLQDFk","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→{\n     2→  \"metadata\": {\n     3→    \"title\": \"Masque of the Red Death - Poe\",\n     4→    \"author\": \"Edgar Allan Poe\",\n     5→    \"source_file\": \"Test_Texts/Masque of the Red Death - Poe.txt\",\n     6→    \"source_format\": \"txt\",\n     7→    \"total_word_count\": 2449,\n     8→    \"total_character_count\": 13811,\n     9→    \"estimated_total_duration_minutes\": 16.286666666666665,\n    10→    \"words_per_minute\": 150\n    11→  },\n    12→  \"structure\": [\n    13→    {\n    14→      \"type\": \"chapter\",\n    15→      \"title\": null,\n    16→      \"index\": 1,\n    17→      \"start_position\": 28,\n    18→      \"end_position\": 13811,\n    19→      \"word_count\": 2443,\n    20→      \"estimated_duration_minutes\": 16.286666666666665,\n    21→      \"confidence\": \"medium\",\n    22→      \"children\": [],\n    23→      \"characters_present\": [\n    24→        \"Prince Prospero\",\n    25→        \"The masked figure (Red Death)\"\n    26→      ],\n    27→      \"summary\": \"The chapter opens with the devastating spread of the 'Red Death,' a horrific plague marked by bleeding pores and rapid death, prompting Prince Prospero to retreat with a thousand courtiers into a secluded, fortified abbey to escape contagion. Inside, he constructs seven elaborately themed rooms—each with uniquely colored stained-glass windows and decor—culminating in a black chamber with blood-red panes and a massive ebony clock that chimes hourly, halting all merriment and instilling dread. During a lavish masked ball, a mysterious figure appears dressed as the Red Death itself, shrouded in grave-cloths and drenched in scarlet stains, causing terror and paralysis among the guests. Prince Prospero, enraged by the blasphemy, pursues the figure through all seven rooms with a dagger, only to collapse and die upon confronting it in th